# Feature model fixtures are compared byte for byte (tabs, CRLF and the absence
# of a trailing newline are all part of what the parity tests assert).
# Git must not normalise them.
* text=auto eol=lf

test/fixtures/** -text
*.uvl -text

# Line templates are byte-for-byte copies of the monolith's
# `linea/server/src/model/services/templates/**`, and their content is what
# gets committed into the GitLab repository of every line created through
# `buildLineScaffold`. The monolith stores them with LF and runs on Linux, so
# LF is what it actually deploys — a CRLF copy would seed every new line with
# different bytes than `linea` does. The wildcard above already normalises
# them; this rule states the requirement explicitly because it is the property
# these files exist to preserve. See test/line/platform-files.test.ts.
src/line/templates/** text eol=lf
